                <pb facs="0522" n="410" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg410"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 24595.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Monroe to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">San
                            Jose</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-05-06"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">May 6, 1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The Government of Costa Rica requires assistance. Did not ask for it. Catastrophe
                    in Cartago by far the worst that the country has had. Horrible calamity.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Monroe</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
